                 ---- carry_forward_rounding_pkg -----------------------------

                 ⚠ SCOPE: the rounding-to-report step, in whole tenths, with no
                 floating point. Rounding matches UTIL_Round exactly: halves
                 away from zero, verified over all 10,011 values of the
                 modelled domain by differential execution against a verbatim
                 harness (2026-09-09). The C loop runs on doubles; this model is
                 a faithful rendering of it for DecimalPlaces <= 1, where the
                 tenths are exactly representable. At 2 or more places the
                 double arithmetic and the integer model can disagree. The C
                 also admits negative prorated values into the loop; amounts
                 here are non-negative.

                 WHAT IS PROVED, graded by the vacuity battery (2026-09-09):
                 Plain_Total, Reported_Total and Balance_Is_Preserved are
                 theorems — the reported total is the true total less exactly
                 the carry, and when the true total lands on the reported
                 precision the reported total equals it. Rounded's
                 postcondition (a multiple of ten) and the postconditions of
                 Residual and Carry_After (each within -5 .. 5) are their result
                 subtypes restated: they prove of an arbitrary result and are
                 graded run-time-only, not theorems. They were written as
                 bounds; by the grade they are not claims.

